  "title": "Sarojini Naidu",
  "summary": "Sarojini Naidu, born in Hyderabad on 13 February 1879, was a poet whose collections include The Golden Threshold (1905). She was the first woman elected president of the Indian National Congress, in 1925, and became governor of the United Provinces in 1947, serving until her death on 2 March 1949.",
